---
import PortfolioPlanningGuide from '../../components/PortfolioPlanningGuide.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "Planning a travertine pool deck replacement",
  "description": "Compare material samples, retained coping and replacement scope before choosing a travertine pool deck.",
  "service": "/services/pool-decks/",
  "serviceLabel": "Pool deck installation",
  "sections": [
    [
      "Define the replacement boundary",
      "Mark the existing surface to be removed, the coping that will stay, and the transitions to doors, steps and walkways. Ask the proposal to distinguish removal and disposal from preparation and installation. A finished-surface photograph does not establish those hidden parts of the scope."
    ],
    [
      "Identify the exact material",
      "Compare a physical sample beside the retained coping and house. Record the manufacturer, product, finish, dimensions and pattern in the proposal. Ask for product-specific guidance on poolside use and care; the word travertine alone does not establish temperature, traction or maintenance performance."
    ],
    [
      "Discuss access and adjoining work",
      "Show the contractor how materials and removed surfaces can reach the work area. Identify screens, irrigation, landscaping and pool equipment that need protection or separate work. Confirm responsibilities for drainage assessment and any applicable approvals before scheduling."
    ],
    [
      "Prepare for the estimate",
      "Bring photographs of the current deck, approximate dimensions, material preferences and any association requirements. Request a written scope with exclusions and scheduling assumptions. Size, price and duration depend on the assessed property; this guide does not quote a completed installation."
    ]
  ]
};
---
<PortfolioPlanningGuide {...guide} />
